  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1242 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nThe jet stream remains split with a northern and southern branch \nwhich usually means zonal flow. That is what we have this week so \nthe trough bringing the precip early Tuesday morning very quickly \nmoves east bringing an end to precipitation chances and a \nresurgence of cool air. The cool air remains in place through \nThursday leaving highs 10-15F below normal. Models are also \ntrending slightly cooler with temperatures Wednesday morning and a\nFreeze Watch will likely be needed soon for much of the area that\nhas not received a freeze to that point. Weak ridging then \ndevelops Friday through the weekend bringing temperatures back up \nto near or slightly above normal. Models are trending deeper with \na low next Friday that digs into Mexico, too far south to provide \nus with precipitation chances.\n\nHennig",
